Although not the first album I'd ever purchased, One On One means a lot
to me;  it was the first album from Cheap Trick after they lost their
trendiness and strong popularity, and one I loved.  I was 7, and found
myself defending my taste in Cheap Trick and other bands for the first
time.  I've had to do it a lot since then, but remember defending
this particular album especially.
That, and I had a crush on the new bassist, Jon Brant.  :)

